From: discfw
Subject: [PATCH] Wait with pause() instead of sleep(UINT_MAX)

With a 32-bit time_t, sleep(UINT_MAX) overflows, nanosleep fails at once and the
loop that keeps the HCI line discipline open spins at 100% CPU.

---
--- a/src/main.c	2026-11-26 22:09:05.160495058 +0100
+++ b/src/main.c	2026-11-26 22:09:05.173650238 +0100
@@ -976,7 +976,7 @@
 		proc_enable_hci();
 
 		while (1) {
-			sleep(UINT_MAX);
+			pause();
 		}
 	}
 
